// Analyzed file list for tasks/openpiton_two_tile_coherence.
//
// Read by two consumers, which is why one list holds every source:
//   * lists/tc_elab.tcl:  analyze -sv12 -f lists/tc_elab.files
//   * taskdefs.slang_args, which filters it into tc_elab.files.slang
//     for the design map.
// v5/round.py appends one `../submission/<web>.sv` line per worker at the
// end, so ORDER MATTERS: the RTL comes first because it carries the
// `include of define.tmp.h / l15.tmp.h / l2.tmp.h whose macros the mesh
// wrapper, the checker and the FT then use, and a worker's file must come
// last so it can reference anything above it.
//
// ONE directory holds the L1.5/L2 RTL, the dynamic-node RTL and the two
// credit transducers, because network_define.v and dmbr_define.v are shipped
// by both upstream trees and neither has an include guard: two copies in one
// single-unit compilation would be two sets of the same macros and no way to
// see which won.
//
// Paths are relative to the package root -- the drivers `cd $task_root`
// before sourcing tc_elab.tcl.

+incdir+rtl/openpiton

// USE_GENERIC_SRAM_IMPLEMENTATION suppresses `SYNTHESIZABLE_BRAM inside
// define.tmp.h, so every sram_* wrapper takes its behavioural array model.
// OpenPiton does not ship bram_1rw_wrapper in the L1.5/L2 filelists, so the
// package would otherwise name a module it does not contain.
+define+USE_GENERIC_SRAM_IMPLEMENTATION

// ---- OpenPiton L1.5 + L2 RTL, PyHP-preprocessed --------------------
